# ------ Template Partials ------

reusable template fragments within a template file
-> can be included in other templates using {% include "dir_with_temp/temp_with_partial.html" %}

{% partialdef user-info %}
    <div id="user-info-{{ user.username }}">
        <h3>{{ user.name }}</h3>
        <p>{{ user.bio }}</p>
    </div>
{% endpartialdef %}

is then rendered with {% partial user-info %}

or straight definition and rendering using {% partialdef user-info inline%} whatever {% endpartialdef %}
-> can also be reused later with {% partial user-info %}

direct access through a view:
def user_info_partial(request, user_id):
    user = get_object_or_404(User, id=user_id)
    return render(request, "authors.html#user-info", {"user": user})
-> only renders the partial, not the whole template (AJAX-style request -> HTMX is modern way of doing so)
-> similarly possible with {% include "authors.html#user-info" %}

context can be adapted to meet demands of partials:
{% with user=featured_author %}
    <h2>Featured Author of the Month</h2>
    {% partial user-info %}
{% endwith %}


